  "review_notes": [
    "The second and third clauses write no interrogative and no negative in Hebrew, so the ASV's repeated Doth/doth/shall and not/not/not are rule 25's distributed realizations of the single הֲ and לֹא of the first clause.",
    "In the first colon the one written he was given to the explicit הוּא and only that to the participle; the competing reading gives he that to the participle and marks הוּא unrepresented.",
    "The margin's Or, this man was read and set aside under rule 38."
